From beb9432e9de8fedacf47ee244a3465bf047d5191 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 20:48:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03338/11362] [outer-loop] arc: coordinated redesign piece 1 --
 cell-recall verify gate (CARNOT_ARC_TRUST_METRIC)

The 0.08-wall root cause is the exact-full-grid-match WorldModelVerifier gate that gates out EVERY
imperfect-but-useful induced world-model (both TTT learned dynamics and e3 LLM induction die there).
Piece 1 of the coordinated redesign: add a GRADED changed-cell-recall companion metric to
WorldModelVerifier (VerifyResult.cell_recall) and gate the e3 verify step on it when
CARNOT_ARC_TRUST_METRIC=cell_recall. Default stays 'exact' -> submitted behavior + parity test (10/10)
unchanged; the e3 attempt now records BOTH verify_accuracy and verify_cell_recall for diagnosis. Probe
script measures whether the gate flips skip->pass on the explorer-failing games. Honest scope: piece 1
is necessary-not-sufficient (pieces 2 divergence-tolerant execute + 3 directed first-win still missing),
so first-win is not expected to move from this alone -- the signal is gate-pass + plan-fire.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
